      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(¬A∧B)⇒¬A.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(¬A∧B)⇒¬A≡¬(¬(¬A∧B))∨¬A.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬(¬A∧B))∨¬A≡(¬A∧B)∨¬A.\n$$\n\nUsing the commutative law, we have\n\n$$\n(¬A∧B)∨¬A≡(B∧¬A)∨¬A\n$$\n\nFinally, by the absorption law, we have\n\n$$\n(B∧¬A)∨¬A≡¬A.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $¬A.$",
